ments, they will all be set to 0.0. Magnetic moments\nwill be converted to the QE units (fraction of valence electrons) using\nany pseudopotential files found, or a best guess for the number of\nvalence electrons.\n\nUnits are not converted for any other input data, so use Quantum ESPRESSO\nunits (Usually Ry or atomic units).\n\nKeys with a dimension (e.g. Hubbard_U(1)) will be incorporated as-is\nso the i should be made to match the output.\n\nImplemented features:', 'title': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/io/formatoptions.html#ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.io.formatoptions', 'qualified_name': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'kind': 'function', 'name': 'write_espresso_in', 'class': None, 'function': 'write_espresso_in', 'chunk_index': 0, 'num_chunks': 5}, 'score': 4.788612365722656, 'vector_score': 0.3862513303756714, 'bm25_score': 22.14366152434766, 'rerank_score': 4.788612365722656}, {'text': '[ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_ph]\nfunction ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_ph\n\nase.io.espresso. write_espresso_ph ( fd , input_data = None , qpts = None , nat_todo_indices = None , ** kwargs ) → None [source] #\n\nFunction that write the input file for a ph.x calculation. Normal namelist\ncards are passed in the input_data dictionary. Which can be either nested\nor flat, ASE style. The q-points are passed in the qpts list. If qplot is\nset to True then qpts is expected to be a list of list|tuple of length 4.\nWhere the first three elements are the coordinates of the q-point in units\nof 2pi/alat and the last element is the weight of the q-point. if qplot is\nset to False then qpts is expected to be a simple list of length 4 (single\nq-point). Finally if ldisp is set to True, the above is discarded and the\nq-points are read from the nq1, nq2, nq3 cards in the input_data dictionary.', 'title': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_ph', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/calculators/espresso.html#ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_ph', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.calculators.espresso', 'qualified_name': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_ph', 'kind': 'function', 'name': 'write_espresso_ph', 'class': None, 'function': 'write_espresso_ph', 'chunk_index': 0, 'num_chunks': 2}, 'score': 3.8318846225738525, 'vector_score': 0.5606080293655396, 'bm25_score': 19.686391838822587, 'rerank_score': 3.8318846225738525}, {'text': "[ase.calculators.espresso.Espresso]\ninput_data: dict A flat or nested dictionary with input parameters for pw.x pseudopotentials: dict A filename for each atomic species, e.g. {'O': 'O.pbe-rrkjus.UPF', 'H': 'H.pbe-rrkjus.UPF'} . A dummy name will be used if none are given. kspacing: float Generate a grid of k-points with this as the minimum distance,\nin A^-1 between them in reciprocal space. If set to None, kpts\nwill be used instead. kpts: (int, int, int), dict, or BandPath If kpts is a tuple (or list) of 3 integers, it is interpreted\nas the dimensions of a Monkhorst-Pack grid. If kpts is set to None , only the Γ-point will be included\nand QE will use routines optimized for Γ-point-only calculations. Compared to Γ-point-only calculations without this optimization\n(i.e. with kpts=(1, 1, 1) ), the memory and CPU requirements\nare typically reduced by half.", 'title': 'ase.calculators.espresso.Espresso', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/calculators/espresso.html#ase.calculators.espresso.Espresso', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.calculators.espresso', 'qualified_name': 'ase.calculators.espresso.Espresso', 'kind': 'class', 'name': 'Espresso', 'class': 'Espresso', 'chunk_index': 1, 'num_chunks': 3}, 'score': 3.3221282958984375, 'vector_score': 0.46052056550979614, 'bm25_score': 10.445077915976368, 'rerank_score': 3.3221282958984375}, {'text': '[ase.io.espresso.read_espresso_in]\nfunction ase.io.espresso.read_espresso_in\n\nase.io.espresso. read_espresso_in ( fileobj ) [source] #\n\nParse a Quantum ESPRESSO input files, ‘.in’, ‘.pwi’.\n\nESPRESSO inputs are generally a fortran-namelist format with custom\nblocks of data. The namelist is parsed as a dict and an atoms object\nis constructed from the included information.\n\nParameters : fileobj ( file | str ) – A file-like object that supports line iteration with the contents\nof the input file, or a filename. Returns : atoms – Structure defined in the input file. Return type : Atoms Raises : KeyError – Raised for missing keys that are required to process the file', 'title': 'ase.io.espresso.read_espresso_in', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/io/formatoptions.html#ase.io.espresso.read_espresso_in', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.io.formatoptions', 'qualified_name': 'ase.io.espresso.read_espresso_in', 'kind': 'function', 'name': 'read_espresso_in', 'class': None, 'function': 'read_espresso_in', 'chunk_index': 0, 'num_chunks': 1}, 'score': 3.0543503761291504, 'vector_score': 0.541608452796936, 'bm25_score': 17.244466524697657, 'rerank_score': 3.0543503761291504}]}

